WEBVTT

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.440
Is it just me, 
or are they staring at us?

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:08.320
Sorry about them.

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:11.650
Second Academy students are bound 
to attract attention.

00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:13.290
Especially lately.

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:14.530
Lately?

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:15.560
Yes.

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:18.420
More and more students 
are completing monster hunts.

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:20.950
First-years in particular.

00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:22.370
<i>I see...</i>

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:24.780
<i>Another result of Matty's teachings.</i>

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:27.090
Now, how can I help you?

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:30.230
We've come to sell goods 
we picked up in the dungeon!

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:31.140
Goodness!

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:35.090
You must be a strong party, 
to be scouring the dungeon!

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:37.420
Is the Crest of Failure bearer 
acting as your porter?

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:39.410
No! Matty is—

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:41.590
Well, I certainly am porting 
my fair share...

00:00:41.590 --> 00:00:42.540
See?

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:48.690
I'd like to sell this.

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:29.000
<b>Episode 3</b>

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:29.000
<b>The Strongest Sage Meets a Dragon.</b>

00:02:30.230 --> 00:02:32.360
A storage spell...

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:35.960
I'd heard rumors, 
but I can't believe it's real!

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:38.300
It shocked us, too!

00:02:39.460 --> 00:02:41.940
Is this all you want to sell?

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:43.730
Oh, plus the magistone...

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:45.100
It's huge!

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:47.430
Is that truly a magistone?

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:50.700
It could qualify as a national treasure.

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:53.710
I got it by defeating the Arc Serpent.

00:02:53.710 --> 00:02:55.870
It's not really big enough, though.

00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:58.410
<i>That's</i> not big enough? 
For what?!

00:02:58.410 --> 00:03:01.500
I need an even bigger one 
to use for the barrier.

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:05.610
Of course, 
I can always get another one.

00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:09.620
You're like 
a national-treasure generator, Matty.

00:03:10.310 --> 00:03:14.150
I'm not sure 
our guild can afford all this.

00:03:15.190 --> 00:03:18.300
I can't believe 
they gave us 750 gold!

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:20.560
I've never seen so much money!

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:22.540
We'll split the proceeds.

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:25.750
250 gold apiece, I suppose?

00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:28.720
250?! We don't deserve that!

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:33.760
Aren't parties supposed to split proceeds 
based on individual contribution?

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:35.190
Are they?

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:40.030
<i>I wouldn't know, since I hardly ever
had a party in my past life.</i>

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:44.260
Matty?

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:46.300
We'd better get back to the academy.

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:47.410
Why—

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:52.320
This magical aura. Could it be...

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:56.250
Yeah, there are two demons 
heading for Second Academy.

00:03:57.140 --> 00:03:59.870
We're almost there, Lord Ashril.

00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:04.340
The human that defeated Devilis 
attends Second Academy, correct?

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:07.100
Yes. Let's go test his mettle.

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:08.470
Just don't go too hard.

00:04:08.470 --> 00:04:10.560
Humans are so fragile, after all.

00:04:11.110 --> 00:04:13.330
One of the demons is on the weak end,

00:04:13.330 --> 00:04:15.580
but the other is stronger than Devilis.

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:19.400
Devilis... 
That's the one you beat, right?!

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:20.320
Yes.

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:23.000
So I'll handle the strong one.

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:25.280
You two take the weaker.

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:27.780
Y-You want us to fight a demon?!

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:29.540
Th-There's no way!

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:30.800
Don't worry.

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:33.620
At the level you are, 
you can put up a good fight.

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:35.040
I have a plan.

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:38.380
I just need you to buy time 
while I take out the stronger one.

00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:44.300
We have to stop the demons 
before they reach the academy.

00:04:45.770 --> 00:04:46.640
Okay.

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:50.600
If you say I can do it, I'll do it!

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:52.150
I shall as well!

00:04:52.150 --> 00:04:53.980
Now that we're a party,

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:56.700
we can't let you shoulder all the burden!

00:04:58.110 --> 00:05:00.940
What's your read, Lord Ashril?

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:03.240
We'll start with a spell from above—

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:05.440
Lord Ashril?

00:05:05.440 --> 00:05:06.820
They're coming.

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:08.740
Impossible!

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:12.420
You startled me there, 
you pathetic human rat.

00:05:12.420 --> 00:05:14.250
But you don't have the power to match!

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:15.970
<i>He's on the weaker end, 
but he's still a demon.</i>

00:05:15.970 --> 00:05:18.420
<i>I can't deal damage without enhancements.</i>

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:22.240
Are you the human who defeated Devilis?

00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:23.700
What if I am?

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:25.210
Yes, a foolish question...

00:05:25.210 --> 00:05:28.510
Whether you are or not, 
you are still a human...

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:30.510
And thus, you must die!

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:33.140
<i>A direct hit from that 
would kill me on the spot.</i>

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:36.120
<i>I don't have much magic power,</i>

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:37.990
<i>but if I burn about half of it...</i>

00:05:39.340 --> 00:05:40.800
Did that get him?

00:05:41.230 --> 00:05:42.440
What?!

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:46.840
<i>If you don't have enough magic, 
just use the enemy's.</i>

00:05:48.840 --> 00:05:50.740
You reflected my spell?

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:52.430
Well played, human.

00:05:52.430 --> 00:05:56.510
<i>Demons these days seem to have
a habit of underestimating humans.</i>

00:05:56.510 --> 00:05:58.870
<i>Sorry to inform you, 
but I didn't reflect it...</i>

00:05:58.870 --> 00:06:00.250
<i>I took control of it!</i>

00:06:01.150 --> 00:06:02.380
Lord Ashril!

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:08.260
<i>Once summoned, these control spheres
stick around until a spell takes them out.</i>

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:10.350
You won't escape, human!

00:06:10.350 --> 00:06:13.240
<i>Control spheres can't stop physical attacks.</i>

00:06:13.240 --> 00:06:15.570
<i>And that's why I need...</i>

00:06:15.570 --> 00:06:16.880
<i>strategy!</i>

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:17.980
Now!

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:22.260
What is it?

00:06:22.260 --> 00:06:23.440
I don't know.

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:25.800
This strange arrow hit me, 
and suddenly I feel—

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:28.360
Yes! It worked!

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:30.460
<i>Lurie enchanted the arrows with a spell</i>

00:06:30.460 --> 00:06:34.150
<i>to disrupt their magic power 
and slow them down.</i>

00:06:35.090 --> 00:06:36.840
I'll deal with this one.

00:06:36.840 --> 00:06:38.370
Deshril, you take them.

00:06:43.980 --> 00:06:46.840
<i>I split them up, just as planned.</i>

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:50.190
I see you've got some odd little tricks 
up your sleeve.

00:06:50.190 --> 00:06:53.620
But there won't be 
any more interference now.

00:06:53.620 --> 00:06:57.310
<i>He thinks he split <i>us</i> up, now?</i>

00:06:57.700 --> 00:06:59.520
Let us end this game.

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:01.980
You cannot reflect this spell!

00:07:01.980 --> 00:07:03.580
<i>A large-scale spell...</i>

00:07:03.580 --> 00:07:05.160
<i>Frightening indeed.</i>

00:07:05.160 --> 00:07:08.200
<i>It'll destroy my control spheres outright.</i>

00:07:08.200 --> 00:07:12.240
<i>But if I fire a spell 
into the casting circle's weak point...</i>

00:07:13.070 --> 00:07:13.700
What?!

00:07:16.440 --> 00:07:17.490
What's wrong?

00:07:17.490 --> 00:07:19.750
First time having a spell canceled on you?

00:07:22.170 --> 00:07:23.750
Impudent brat!

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:26.750
But don't let success go 
to your head, human!

00:07:29.770 --> 00:07:30.920
Why...

00:07:31.860 --> 00:07:33.140
Why can't I hit you?!

00:07:33.890 --> 00:07:35.630
<i>That's very simple!</i>

00:07:35.630 --> 00:07:37.850
<i>Your swordsmanship...</i>

00:07:37.850 --> 00:07:39.520
<i>just isn't up to snuff!</i>

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:44.960
<i>I picked up so much combat experience 
in my past life.</i>

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:47.230
<i>There's no way he could match up.</i>

00:07:47.230 --> 00:07:49.110
In that case...

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:51.240
Hey! Where do you think you're going?

00:07:57.870 --> 00:08:00.320
A flight spell won't save you, either.

00:08:00.320 --> 00:08:02.620
I have full control 
over all your casting.

00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:05.250
What manner of beast are you?!

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:09.590
I will not abide a demon 
calling me a beast!

00:08:14.010 --> 00:08:15.310
You fell for it!

00:08:15.310 --> 00:08:17.500
The fact that you went out of your way 
to cancel my spell

00:08:17.500 --> 00:08:20.600
was a sign that 
you really didn't want me casting it!

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:22.440
<i>A concealed cast...</i>

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:26.240
<i>He was constructing the casting circle 
while we crossed swords, then?</i>

00:08:29.080 --> 00:08:31.940
That spell came from Lord Ashril!

00:08:39.480 --> 00:08:41.700
You dodged that one, too...

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:45.290
But at least I rid myself 
of those annoying spheres!

00:08:45.290 --> 00:08:48.290
I'll let you go this time.

00:08:48.290 --> 00:08:50.170
But the next time we meet—

00:08:52.460 --> 00:08:54.010
<i>An occlusion orb.</i>

00:08:54.010 --> 00:08:57.870
<i>A spell to contract the body's 
magical power conduits and stymie the flow.</i>

00:08:57.870 --> 00:09:00.010
<i>It's usually no more than a nuisance...</i>

00:09:00.270 --> 00:09:03.580
<i>But if cast on someone concentrating 
vast amounts of magic power</i>

00:09:03.580 --> 00:09:05.280
<i>for a spell like Full Flight,</i>

00:09:05.280 --> 00:09:08.270
<i>the magic is denied an outlet 
and runs wild within them.</i>

00:09:10.820 --> 00:09:15.330
If you don't have enough magic, 
just use the enemy's.

00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:17.610
And now—

00:09:19.390 --> 00:09:22.490
You noticed... that, too?!

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:28.660
<i>He was just about 
to cast a demon-exclusive spell</i>

00:09:28.660 --> 00:09:33.080
<i>that gives up one's life 
to summon a vast horde of monsters.</i>

00:09:33.080 --> 00:09:35.250
<i>I sealed it before he could.</i>

00:09:39.780 --> 00:09:42.240
You've started quite a panic, haven't you?

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:44.430
You're a terrible thorn 
in my side, you know.

00:09:44.430 --> 00:09:46.440
I don't give a damn.

00:09:48.770 --> 00:09:51.520
That's one successful dispatch, then.

00:09:53.570 --> 00:09:54.610
Alma!

00:09:56.010 --> 00:09:56.570
Go!

00:09:56.860 --> 00:09:58.840
More of those strange arrows?!

00:10:00.960 --> 00:10:01.730
Now!

00:10:01.730 --> 00:10:02.600
Right!

00:10:03.260 --> 00:10:04.700
Run!

00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:07.550
Damn! They got away again!

00:10:07.550 --> 00:10:09.670
They're doing rather well.

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:13.370
Release a disruption arrow 
at the demon as it approaches,

00:10:13.370 --> 00:10:15.110
then quickly withdraw.

00:10:15.110 --> 00:10:18.770
They're maintaining a distance 
from which they can dodge all its attacks.

00:10:19.500 --> 00:10:21.470
I suppose I should finish things off, though.

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:25.110
Impudent human brats...

00:10:25.110 --> 00:10:27.810
But once Lord Ashril and I reunite—

00:10:27.810 --> 00:10:28.850
Heya!

00:10:29.210 --> 00:10:30.510
Matty!

00:10:30.510 --> 00:10:32.180
What are you doing here?!

00:10:32.180 --> 00:10:33.660
What happened to Lord Ashril?

00:10:33.660 --> 00:10:36.740
Your little friend? 
He's on the ground, over there.

00:10:36.740 --> 00:10:39.440
What?! You defeated Lord Ashril?

00:10:39.440 --> 00:10:40.740
That can't be true!

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:43.360
In the mood to find out?

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:48.330
That spell... Can it be?!

00:10:48.330 --> 00:10:53.340
<i>Yes, the light of death 
that can slay a demon in one strike.</i>

00:10:53.340 --> 00:10:56.880
<i>Actually, it's a simple light spell 
designed to look like that.</i>

00:10:56.880 --> 00:11:00.320
<i>I can't cast the real thing 
at my current magic levels.</i>

00:11:00.320 --> 00:11:02.150
Well? What now?

00:11:02.150 --> 00:11:03.670
You beast!

00:11:03.670 --> 00:11:04.930
This isn't over!

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:06.470
Alma! Fire!

00:11:06.470 --> 00:11:07.620
But he's too far—

00:11:07.620 --> 00:11:08.520
It'll work!

00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:09.680
Okay!

00:11:09.680 --> 00:11:10.400
Lurie!

00:11:10.400 --> 00:11:11.300
Right!

00:11:12.860 --> 00:11:13.860
Matty!

00:11:14.360 --> 00:11:17.230
<i>I can't match a Full Flight 
in my current state...</i>

00:11:17.230 --> 00:11:19.100
<i>But an arrow can!</i>

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:22.910
Stay back! Stay back!

00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:35.000
And another successful dispatch.

00:11:35.820 --> 00:11:37.500
That was amazing, Matty!

00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:40.100
I can't believe we fought a demon!

00:11:40.100 --> 00:11:42.710
You landed almost all your hits on it, too!

00:11:42.710 --> 00:11:45.310
Only thanks to your enchanted arrows!

00:11:45.310 --> 00:11:49.400
But that's only thanks 
to the spells Matty taught me!

00:11:49.920 --> 00:11:51.230
Matty?

00:11:51.230 --> 00:11:52.700
Were those demons?

00:11:51.230 --> 00:11:52.700
An academy student defeated demons?

00:11:52.700 --> 00:11:53.740
All by himself?

00:11:53.740 --> 00:11:57.020
No, with two others! 
Beautiful girls!

00:11:57.560 --> 00:11:58.420
<i>This isn't good.</i>

00:11:58.420 --> 00:12:00.140
<i>There are too many of them.</i>

00:12:00.140 --> 00:12:02.150
<i>This is definitely going 
to get complicated.</i>

00:12:02.580 --> 00:12:04.640
What should we do, Matty?

00:12:04.640 --> 00:12:08.880
There's only one thing to do 
when surrounded by enemies you can't slay.

00:12:08.880 --> 00:12:10.470
Uh, "enemies"?

00:12:10.470 --> 00:12:14.690
Activate a movement spell 
and aim for a hole in their ranks.

00:12:14.690 --> 00:12:16.970
In this case, that means up!

00:12:16.970 --> 00:12:20.500
But... we can't fly!

00:12:20.500 --> 00:12:23.180
That's right. 
I haven't taught you that yet.

00:12:23.540 --> 00:12:24.560
Sorry about this!

00:12:24.560 --> 00:12:26.200
M-Matty?!

00:12:26.200 --> 00:12:27.300
The thing to do now...

00:12:28.020 --> 00:12:29.060
is run!

00:12:29.060 --> 00:12:30.700
M-Matty...

00:12:30.700 --> 00:12:32.480
Hey, look at that!

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:34.000
It's so pretty!

00:12:43.480 --> 00:12:46.570
Let me congratulate you 
on a job well done.

00:12:46.570 --> 00:12:48.480
Th-That's the king!

00:12:48.480 --> 00:12:49.620
The real king!

00:12:49.890 --> 00:12:51.800
I'll get right to the point.

00:12:51.800 --> 00:12:54.040
Matthias. What do you ask for?

00:12:54.530 --> 00:12:56.320
If it is national treasures you seek,

00:12:56.320 --> 00:12:58.130
I'll give you run 
of the storehouse once more.

00:12:58.890 --> 00:13:01.680
<i>There's nothing left 
in the storehouse that I want.</i>

00:13:01.680 --> 00:13:04.240
<i>Authority over Second Academy, perhaps?</i>

00:13:04.240 --> 00:13:09.810
<i>No, since I'm planning to leave the academy 
once the demons are dealt with...</i>

00:13:11.160 --> 00:13:13.060
Give me dungeons, then.

00:13:13.060 --> 00:13:14.600
As many as you can.

00:13:14.600 --> 00:13:17.400
Very well. 
I'll find you as many as I can.

00:13:17.400 --> 00:13:18.650
<i>Excellent!</i>

00:13:18.650 --> 00:13:20.680
More dungeons, eh?

00:13:20.680 --> 00:13:22.690
You two also contributed to this.

00:13:22.980 --> 00:13:25.740
Speak your request, and it shall be yours.

00:13:25.740 --> 00:13:27.920
Sir! I want money!

00:13:27.920 --> 00:13:29.480
You can never have too much money,

00:13:29.480 --> 00:13:31.700
and you can always find 
a use for it later!

00:13:33.300 --> 00:13:35.910
Very well! I shall see to it.

00:13:35.910 --> 00:13:39.480
<i>Alma's her usual self, even around the king.</i>

00:13:39.480 --> 00:13:41.550
I suppose I'll have the same...

00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:42.570
Indeed.

00:13:42.570 --> 00:13:45.100
I shall provide you both just compensation.

00:13:45.100 --> 00:13:47.320
We can decide 
on the precise amount later—

00:13:47.320 --> 00:13:49.260
If I may, Your Majesty.

00:13:50.920 --> 00:13:52.580
Hey, come on out.

00:13:52.580 --> 00:13:53.620
Matthias?

00:13:53.620 --> 00:13:55.770
You can't hide from me, you know.

00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:59.880
All that magic power you're pumping out 
is just giving you away.

00:13:59.880 --> 00:14:01.900
Is there someone else here?

00:14:01.900 --> 00:14:04.640
Yes, demons are watching us.

00:14:04.640 --> 00:14:07.110
Though they're not technically here.

00:14:07.110 --> 00:14:09.140
Cat still got your tongue?

00:14:09.140 --> 00:14:10.330
All right, then...

00:14:10.330 --> 00:14:12.520
I'll just have to force you to talk!

00:14:15.520 --> 00:14:17.620
<i>That went well.</i>

00:14:17.620 --> 00:14:20.920
Majesty! Did you recognize that voice?

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:23.480
Erhard, former Captain of the Mages' Order!

00:14:23.480 --> 00:14:26.510
Did he arrange a way 
to listen in on this room?

00:14:26.510 --> 00:14:29.790
Yes, it's a fixed magical interface,

00:14:29.790 --> 00:14:32.230
a spell allowing 
for long-range surveillance.

00:14:32.230 --> 00:14:33.920
And you slayed the surveillant?!

00:14:33.920 --> 00:14:37.200
I dealt a little damage, 
but I doubt I finished him off.

00:14:37.200 --> 00:14:40.850
So the demons have been listening in 
on all our plans?

00:14:40.850 --> 00:14:41.870
Your Majesty.

00:14:41.870 --> 00:14:47.560
348 kilometers west 
and 4425 kilometers north of this palace...

00:14:47.560 --> 00:14:50.630
Is there anything special in that location?

00:14:50.630 --> 00:14:55.040
I felt a reaction from that region 
when I destroyed the magical interface.

00:14:56.160 --> 00:14:59.500
A village that was once destroyed by demons.

00:14:59.800 --> 00:15:03.140
The demons are hiding out in those ruins.

00:15:03.140 --> 00:15:06.800
Given the reverberations in the voice, 
they're probably indoors.

00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:10.600
Your spell told you all that?

00:15:10.600 --> 00:15:12.900
What do we do, Matthias?

00:15:12.900 --> 00:15:16.060
The demons have been so kind 
as to give us their location.

00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:18.000
We really should pay them a visit.

00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:19.900
But it's so far away!

00:15:19.900 --> 00:15:22.240
Wouldn't it take half a year 
to travel that far?

00:15:22.240 --> 00:15:23.470
True.

00:15:23.470 --> 00:15:26.540
Even with a teleportation spell, 
my crest couldn't take us far.

00:15:26.540 --> 00:15:29.030
You can use teleportation spells?!

00:15:29.030 --> 00:15:32.080
Yeah, but it's useless right now,

00:15:32.080 --> 00:15:34.050
so I'll have to figure out 
another way to get there.

00:15:34.050 --> 00:15:35.450
R-Right...

00:15:35.720 --> 00:15:38.840
Did he just... 
call a legendary spell "useless"?

00:15:45.030 --> 00:15:48.700
The headmaster seemed
very enthusiastic, didn't he?

00:15:48.700 --> 00:15:53.470
Yes, he was over the moon 
about gathering materials for the barrier!

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:58.960
Let's round up 1.5 tons of mithril 
before Matthias and his party return!

00:15:58.960 --> 00:16:00.350
Yeah!

00:16:00.790 --> 00:16:04.540
<i>He was about to rope me 
into teaching tons of special classes,</i>

00:16:04.540 --> 00:16:06.060
<i>so I feel that I'm getting off easy.</i>

00:16:06.450 --> 00:16:10.850
So, how are we going 
to get to the demons?

00:16:10.850 --> 00:16:13.340
I told you. 
You'll find out when we get there.

00:16:13.340 --> 00:16:15.520
I think you'll be pleasantly surprised!

00:16:15.520 --> 00:16:19.510
You certainly are full of surprises, Matty...

00:16:19.510 --> 00:16:21.030
What's that supposed to mean?

00:16:22.430 --> 00:16:26.680
<i>Although, the associated signature 
has certainly weakened...</i>

00:16:26.680 --> 00:16:29.550
<i>I just hope we can still get 
a ride out of this.</i>

00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:31.680
Oh, here we are.

00:16:32.660 --> 00:16:34.550
W-We are?

00:16:34.550 --> 00:16:38.810
This looks an awful lot 
like a certain legendary creature...

00:16:39.860 --> 00:16:41.860
Think of it as a fancy carriage.

00:16:41.860 --> 00:16:43.140
One that happens to breathe fire.

00:16:43.140 --> 00:16:45.810
B-But isn't that...

00:16:45.810 --> 00:16:48.270
A dragon?!

00:16:48.270 --> 00:16:50.980
More precisely, 
Iris the Darkness Dragon.

00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:54.990
You mean one of 
those legendary kingdom-destroyers?!

00:16:55.350 --> 00:16:56.760
I'll negotiate.

00:16:56.760 --> 00:16:58.580
You two wait here.

00:16:58.580 --> 00:16:59.830
"Negotiate"?!

00:17:00.460 --> 00:17:03.050
<i>Iris the Darkness Dragon was a member 
of the dragons</i>

00:17:03.050 --> 00:17:05.120
<i>that picked a fight with me 
in my past life.</i>

00:17:05.400 --> 00:17:09.290
<i>She surrendered early on, 
so I let her go.</i>

00:17:09.790 --> 00:17:11.880
<i>Iris and I go a long way back.</i>

00:17:11.880 --> 00:17:14.470
<i>I'm sure she'll be happy 
to see me again.</i>

00:17:14.920 --> 00:17:16.600
Intruder.

00:17:16.600 --> 00:17:18.700
This is my domain.

00:17:18.700 --> 00:17:22.100
I did not grant you ingress.

00:17:22.100 --> 00:17:22.910
Eh?

00:17:22.910 --> 00:17:25.990
But I do not seek unnecessary death.

00:17:25.990 --> 00:17:27.840
I will allow you to leave.

00:17:27.840 --> 00:17:32.350
But if you take one more step inward, 
you will die.

00:17:32.350 --> 00:17:34.940
<i>She doesn't remember me, then?</i>

00:17:34.940 --> 00:17:36.940
Die!

00:17:36.940 --> 00:17:38.200
Matty!

00:17:38.480 --> 00:17:40.320
<i>Dragon's Breath, eh?</i>

00:17:40.320 --> 00:17:42.460
<i>But with such an efficient, 
intricate casting circle,</i>

00:17:42.460 --> 00:17:45.240
<i>if you can just strike the weak point...</i>

00:17:48.540 --> 00:17:49.560
Er?

00:17:50.040 --> 00:17:53.800
Was that a disruption spell?

00:17:53.800 --> 00:17:55.190
Yes, it was.

00:17:55.190 --> 00:17:57.560
Wait, you speak dragon?!

00:17:57.560 --> 00:17:59.790
Come on. 
It's common knowledge.

00:18:01.020 --> 00:18:05.060
D-Do you know a man named Gaius, 
by chance?

00:18:05.060 --> 00:18:08.760
He died a few thousand years ago 
and claimed he was going to reincarnate...

00:18:08.760 --> 00:18:11.980
Know him? I'm his reincarnation!

00:18:11.980 --> 00:18:14.720
Eek! I'm so sorry!

00:18:14.720 --> 00:18:18.780
I didn't realize it was you, Lord Gaius!

00:18:18.780 --> 00:18:21.390
This is all just a big misunderstanding!

00:18:21.390 --> 00:18:24.140
Please, don't kill me!

00:18:22.470 --> 00:18:25.270
Look at that! The dragon's groveling!

00:18:25.270 --> 00:18:27.310
Hush, Alma! It'll hear you!

00:18:27.310 --> 00:18:28.500
You're safe. I promise.

00:18:28.500 --> 00:18:31.250
I didn't come here to hurt you.

00:18:32.480 --> 00:18:34.420
Y-You didn't?

00:18:34.720 --> 00:18:38.470
I need to slay some demons, 
but they're rather far away.

00:18:38.470 --> 00:18:40.330
Could you take us there on your back?

00:18:40.330 --> 00:18:41.960
Sure, but...

00:18:41.960 --> 00:18:44.640
Why not use a teleportation spell?

00:18:45.340 --> 00:18:47.480
This is my crest now.

00:18:47.480 --> 00:18:49.430
The Fourth Crest, huh?

00:18:49.430 --> 00:18:51.600
That's the crest you liked very much,

00:18:51.600 --> 00:18:55.580
but that you should 
really never be allowed to have!

00:18:55.580 --> 00:18:57.360
Who exactly do you take me for?

00:18:57.360 --> 00:19:00.010
Matty! Think we could get an update?

00:19:00.010 --> 00:19:01.900
I've got us a ride.

00:19:01.900 --> 00:19:03.280
You can come on over.

00:19:03.280 --> 00:19:04.740
T-Truly?!

00:19:04.740 --> 00:19:08.020
Actually, I never said I could take you—

00:19:08.020 --> 00:19:08.720
Hm?

00:19:08.720 --> 00:19:12.210
Eek! Not <i>"would"</i>! "Could"!

00:19:12.760 --> 00:19:15.750
Look at my wings!

00:19:15.750 --> 00:19:17.500
That's awful.

00:19:17.500 --> 00:19:19.760
How did they get so torn up?

00:19:20.210 --> 00:19:22.530
After you died to reincarnate,

00:19:22.530 --> 00:19:27.000
a magic reactor 
in a human kingdom exploded.

00:19:27.000 --> 00:19:29.990
This incited explosions 
in other magical reactors

00:19:29.990 --> 00:19:31.980
and sent humans back 
to the stone age.

00:19:31.980 --> 00:19:35.940
That explains the regression in civilization.

00:19:35.940 --> 00:19:39.150
Do you think you could fix my wings?

00:19:39.150 --> 00:19:43.530
I have the Fourth Crest now, 
so it won't be a perfect fix, but...

00:19:46.680 --> 00:19:48.690
That should be enough 
for you to fly, right?

00:19:48.690 --> 00:19:51.290
Yes! Thank you so much!

00:19:51.290 --> 00:19:53.880
I think we should start talking 
in human language now.

00:19:53.880 --> 00:19:55.540
But my name is Matthias now.

00:19:55.540 --> 00:19:57.780
Keep my reincarnation between us, 
if you please.

00:19:57.780 --> 00:19:59.050
Certainly!

00:19:59.520 --> 00:20:00.870
All right now...

00:20:01.470 --> 00:20:03.020
Lurie, Alma.

00:20:03.020 --> 00:20:04.750
There's no need to be frightened.

00:20:04.750 --> 00:20:06.850
Go on. Make pleasantries.

00:20:06.850 --> 00:20:08.210
It's a pleasure to meet you!

00:20:08.210 --> 00:20:11.270
Would you be Matthias's comrades, then?

00:20:11.730 --> 00:20:14.400
Oh, did they not hear me?

00:20:14.400 --> 00:20:15.770
Let's see...

00:20:15.770 --> 00:20:19.730
Th-The dragon talked!

00:20:21.230 --> 00:20:24.260
Hold on tight, now!

00:20:28.120 --> 00:20:31.020
My first flight in five thousand years!

00:20:31.020 --> 00:20:32.080
What a feeling!

00:20:32.380 --> 00:20:36.290
I'm riding a dragon. 
It's like a fairy tale!

00:20:36.290 --> 00:20:38.340
We're so high up!

00:20:38.620 --> 00:20:42.640
Where would you like me to go, Matthias?

00:20:42.640 --> 00:20:45.640
4500 kilometers in this direction.

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:47.660
Fly as fast as humans can bear,

00:20:47.660 --> 00:20:50.060
but maintain an altitude 
no more than 1000 meters.

00:20:50.360 --> 00:20:53.100
4500 kilometers is a hop, skip, and a jump!

00:20:53.100 --> 00:20:57.730
Now here I go, 
as fast as humans can bear!

00:20:57.730 --> 00:20:58.730
Wait!

00:21:00.580 --> 00:21:01.870
What's wrong with you?!

00:21:01.870 --> 00:21:03.700
That's my line!

00:21:03.700 --> 00:21:06.590
How fast were you planning on 
going just now?

00:21:06.590 --> 00:21:09.440
I believe you said, 
"Fly as fast as humans can bear."

00:21:09.440 --> 00:21:11.730
I know I can't base that speed on Gaius,

00:21:11.730 --> 00:21:14.300
so I thought I'd base it 
on his old friend Reuter.

00:21:14.300 --> 00:21:17.000
So, basically as fast as you can go.

00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:21.200
Is she talking about Gaius, God of Magic, 
and Reuter, God of Swords?

00:21:21.200 --> 00:21:27.720
This really might be the same Iris 
the Darkness Dragon from the legends.

00:21:27.720 --> 00:21:30.310
<i>So the gods they worship in this era</i>

00:21:30.310 --> 00:21:34.060
<i>share names with my old self 
and my friend Reuter?</i>

00:21:34.500 --> 00:21:37.650
<i>I suppose there are truths 
that only gods know.</i>

00:21:38.020 --> 00:21:38.800
Iris.

00:21:38.800 --> 00:21:41.500
Roll it back to one five-hundredth 
of the speed you were about to go.

00:21:41.500 --> 00:21:43.610
It'll tear apart your wings otherwise.

00:21:43.610 --> 00:21:46.110
Consider it done!

00:21:47.240 --> 00:21:48.720
Okay, let's go!

00:21:48.720 --> 00:21:51.800
Next stop: The village 
where the demons are hiding!

00:21:51.800 --> 00:21:52.890
All right!

00:23:26.120 --> 00:23:29.030
A pleasure to make your acquaintance!

00:23:29.030 --> 00:23:31.000
Yes. What's wrong, you two?

00:23:31.000 --> 00:23:32.260
W-Well...

00:23:32.260 --> 00:23:33.260
Well?

00:23:33.260 --> 00:23:36.970
Th-The dragon is talking!

00:23:36.970 --> 00:23:39.930
You're kind of hurting my feelings, now...

00:23:36.970 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Episode 4
The Strongest Sage Infiltrates.</b>
